\title{#{\sigma}-embedding}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Let #{L/K}, #{M/K'} be field extensions, and let #{\sigma \colon K \to K'} be a field embedding. A \em{#{\sigma}-embedding} #{\tau \colon L \to M} is an embedding which extends #{\sigma}, i.e. #{\tau(x) = \sigma(x)} for all #{x \in K}.}

##{\begin{CD} L @>{\tau}>> M \\ @AAA @AAA \\ K @>{\sigma}>> K' \end{CD}}

\p{Equivalently, #{\sigma = \tau|_K} is the restriction of #{\tau} to #{K}.}
